# Load-bearing rules for shared:linear-issue.
# Each line survives any trim. Prose, rationale and the worked example do not.
# Patterns are deliberately loose on wording and strict on the operative token,
# so a rewrite passes and a deletion fails.

title format is "<type> - <App>: <sentence>" :: <type>` ?- ?`?<App>|<type> - <App>
all six issue types are named :: bug.*feat.*chore.*docs.*spec.*trend
spec is decided by the presence of decisions, not by findings or a fix :: spec.*only if.*decisions
priority lives in the field, never the body :: [Pp]riority.*field
priority 1 covers production users, data, money or security now :: `?1`? Urgent
priority 4 covers docs, chore and trend :: `?4`? Low
a blocking issue inherits the blocked issue's priority :: blocks.*takes|takes the blocked
relations go in fields, never prose :: [Rr]elations.*field|blockedBy
a non-issue dependency becomes an Open or Risk line :: (Open|Risk).*line
the short-form word cap is 180 and is measured with wc -w :: 180 words
the cut order is rationale, narrative, restated code, filler :: rationale.*narrative|rationale, the narrative
instructions are never cut to make the cap :: never cut
over the cap with only instructions left, it stays one ticket and you say so :: stays one ticket|runs over
one ticket by default; split needs independent closure AND ordering :: closed without the others
a split issue is linked with blocks :: link(ed)? it with `?blocks|linked with `?blocks
length alone never splits a ticket :: not length|not bullet count
submit with save_issue :: save_issue
sub-issues only for a spec with ordered slices, or on request :: [Ss]ub-issues.*spec|only for a spec
sub-issues attach via parentId :: parentId
sub-issue title format is "feat - <App>: <slice>" :: feat - <App>: <slice>
sub-issues carry no Decisions table and no Risk line :: no Decisions table
a bug or task is never split into sub-issues :: never split into sub-issues
the short form carries Evidence, Refs, Risk, Open, Fix and Acceptance :: Evidence:.*|Refs:|Risk:|Open:
acceptance is capped at three :: at most three
the Open line is capped at two :: at most two
a spec adds a Decisions table of Question, Decision, Why :: Question \| Decision \| Why
the Decisions table sits between Open and Fix :: between the Open line and Fix
a spec has no word cap :: No word cap|no word cap
no Context, Why it matters, or How this was found sections :: ## Context
severity is not repeated in the body :: [Ss]everity lives in the priority field
never lower a spec by deleting its decisions :: [Nn]ever lower a spec
never raise a bug to a spec to keep rationale :: never raise a bug
the count is measured, not estimated :: measured, not estimated
the cap bounds explanation, never scope :: bounds explanation
a sub-issue never repeats the parent's Problem or Evidence :: never repeats the parent
